fn format_parse_error(input: &str, pos: usize, msg: &str, _kind: &str)->String{
    // msg is like "Expected expression, found '|'" or "Expected identifier, found '.'", etc.
    // Format: "error: {msg}\n  --> query\n  |\n1 | {input}\n{spaces}^...  {kind}\n\n" where kind is "unexpected token" or "unexpected character" or "invalid filter", etc.
    // For parser errors, kind is "unexpected token" (for most), except invalid filter (which is "invalid filter") and unterminated (which is "string not closed")? Actually invalid filter error is "error: Invalid filter: expected filter pattern or index\n  --> query\n  |\n1 | .h[\n       ^  invalid filter\n\n" with kind "invalid filter" (not "unexpected token"). Good. Handled separately.
    // For parser errors here, kind is "unexpected token" (as passed in _kind? Actually our calls pass "unexpected token" as kind. Good.
